  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining humanitarian hubs in Nigeria (SHHiN)Sustaining humanitarian hubs in Nigeria (SHHiN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For over 13 years, north-east Nigeria has faced a protracted humanitarian crisis marked by conflict, violence, and insecurity, significantly restricting humanitarian access. In Borno State, unsafe road travel due to attacks and abductions by Non-State Armed Groups (NSAGs) poses severe risks to aid delivery. To address these challenges, IOM manages eight humanitarian hubs across in Borno State, serving as secure operational bases for humanitarian actors. These hubs provide safe accommodation, office space, internet access, and meeting facilities, enabling humanitarian agencies to operate in high-risk areas.This Action aims to ensure the sustained operation and maintenance of the seven deep-field humanitarian hubs located in Bama, Banki, Ngala, Damasak, Dikwa, Gwoza, and Monguno. These hubs are crucial for enabling humanitarian partners to continue delivering vital assistance and support to conflict-affected communities in north-east Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
